'''2.''' Any higher proposition, obtained by generalization and induction from the observation of individual instances; the enunciation of a general fact; an empirical law. {{smaller|This use originated with Bacon, influenced probably by the employment of ''axiom'' by the Stoics to mean any proposition.}} '''3†.''' In ''logic'', a proposition, whether true or false: a use of the term which originated with Zeno the Stoic. ='''Syn. 1.''' {{smaller|''Maxim'', ''Truism'', etc. See ''aphorism''.}}

